    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Carroll delight in presenting this dream farmhouse to the market. A charming farmhouse set in a peaceful, rural location at Deerpark, Drumirril. The property offers a wonderful opportunity to create a comfortable family home in a superb attractive countryside setting, with generous grounds of .54 acres with excellent potential for further development or modernisation, subject to the necessary planning permissions. Also included are some stone out buildings, ideal for conversion for home office or studio.\n\nLocated just 15 minutes from Carrickmacross and 25 minutes to Dundalk, the property is set in a hugely historically significant area, Deerpark is home to numerous Megalithic tombs and rock art. Inniskeen in famous in history and is known throughout Ireland and beyond as Patrick Kavanagh Country with the Patrick Kavanagh Resource Centre being the centre point of this quaint village.\n\nIdeally suited to those seeking a quiet, rural lifestyle while remaining within convenient reach of local amenities and surrounding towns. The property combines traditional farmhouse character with the potential to create a modern home tailored to individual requirements.\n\nViewing of this fantastic property is highly recommended!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGROUND FLOOR - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - 1.04m x 5.39m\n\n\nLiving Room - 3.41m x 3.45m\n\n\nSitting Room - 3.19m x 4.36m\n\n\nKitchen - 2.71m x 2.59m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.52m x 2.37m\n\n\nFIRST FLOOR - \n\n\nBedroom - 4.31m x 3.32m\n\n\nBedroom - 3.93m x 4.35m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.56m x 2.37m\n\n\n - \nTOTAL FLOOR AREA: 77.9 sq.m. / 839 sq.ft. approx.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Oil fired central heating </li><li>Off street parking </li><li>Range of sheds</li><li>West facing rear garden</ul>"
      },
